Description: python3-setuptools is a build dependency, not a test-only one
 debian/control marks python3-setuptools <!nocheck>, but setup.py imports
 setuptools (falling back to distutils, which Python 3.12 removed) for every
 step, even "setup.py clean". So a nocheck build fails at its first step with
 "No module named 'setuptools'". Drop the <!nocheck> restriction.
Author: Yohane Linux Maintainers <aqours@koiren.ai>
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/debian/control	2026-11-24 05:34:26.896577695 +0000
+++ b/debian/control	2026-11-24 05:34:26.896577695 +0000
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
                help2man,
                python3-all-dev,
                python3-numpy <!nocheck>,
-               python3-setuptools <!nocheck>,
+               python3-setuptools,
 Build-Depends-Indep: dh-sequence-sphinxdoc,
                      python3-sphinx,
                      python3-sphinx-issues,
